From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: the pointer's motion at a shown edge reaches raw input
 (Wine patch 0930)

In a display mode smaller than the screen, the stick's pointer stopped
at the shown edge and no motion was sent past it. A game that moves a
pointer of its own by DirectInput's motion stopped short of its far
side (Sacred Underworld at 1024x768, a little before the right edge).
The pointer still stops at the edge, and its motion still reaches raw
input, as on Windows.
